//   aggregators for current listings).
// - Storekeeper content is grounded in a real, near-identical posting for
//   the same role at a comparable Rwandan public teaching hospital
//   (Storekeeper, Neuro Psychiatric Teaching Hospital Caraes Ndera,
//   greatrwandajobs.com /job-Storekeeper-job-at-Neuro-Psychiatric-Teaching-
//   Hospital-Caraes-Ndera-Ndera-Hospital-38311 — FIFO replenishment, stock
//   reconciliation, weekly ordering, complaints register, key-holder
//   register, shelf-vs-database spot checks), plus standard public-sector
//   and medical-store inventory practice (ABC analysis, EOQ, min/max
//   levels, FEFO for perishable/expiring medical items, segregation of
//   duties) and verified Rwandan institutional facts (Rwanda Medical
//   Supply Ltd (RMS) — the state body procuring, storing and distributing
//   medical commodities to public facilities since 2020; Rwanda Public
//   Procurement Authority (RPPA)).
// - Radiographer content is grounded in a real, current CHUB posting in
//   the same imaging department (Ultrasound Technician, Central
//   University Hospital of Butare (CHUB), kigalistore.com
//   /jobs/ultrasound-technician-at-central-university-hospital-of-butare-
//   chub — radiographic/imaging exams, radiation-protection principles of
//   justification/optimisation/dose limits, daily equipment QA, infection
//   control, "valid practice license issued by the professional council
//   in Rwanda"), a comparable current Radiographer posting at a sister
//   national referral hospital (Radiographer, King Faisal Hospital,
//   greatrwandajobs.com — A1 diploma in Medical Imaging Sciences,
//   professional registration, 3 years' experience), the verified law
//   establishing Rwanda's professional licensing body (Law N°46/2012 of
//   14/01/2013 establishing the Rwanda Allied Health Professions Council,
//   RAHPC), the verified radiation-equipment regulator (RURA, under Law
//   N°59/2017, licenses diagnostic radiology/CT/mobile X-ray equipment),
//   a verified 2026 news fact (CHUB installed Rwanda's first MRI machine
//   located outside Kigali), and standard, internationally accepted
//   radiography/radiation-safety/radiobiology knowledge (ALARA, time-
//   distance-shielding, inverse square law, positioning conventions),
//   which needs no country-specific citation.
// - "Level 8.II" (Storekeeper) and "Level 4.II" (Radiographer) follow
//   Rwanda's public-service job classification, where a lower level
//   number corresponds to a higher required qualification (verified
//   pattern: a Level 4.II post at Gakenke District required an A0
//   bachelor's degree). Level 8.II therefore corresponds to a lower
//   (A2-equivalent, e.g. advanced-diploma/technical-secondary) stock-
